-- Advisor "unindexed_foreign_keys": 1,039 foreign key constraints across the schema have no
-- covering index, which forces sequential scans (or full-table locks on the referencing side
-- during parent-row updates/deletes) once real data volume shows up. This tenant is a demo with
-- near-zero rows today, so the cost isn't visible yet, but the index is cheap to add now and
-- expensive to discover missing later once tables are populated.
--
-- Purely additive (CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS): does not change query results, RLS behavior, or
-- grants. Every statement below was generated directly from live pg_constraint/pg_attribute data
-- (schema, table, and column names came from the catalog, not retyped), covering all 1,039
-- constraints identified by the advisor. Index names are derived from each constraint's own
-- name (already unique per table) with the `_fkey` suffix swapped for `_idx`, truncated to fit
-- Postgres's 63-byte identifier limit; verified zero collisions across all 1,039 before applying.
